    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d979">

                <pb facs="1036" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg750"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McAdoo</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 13, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of Mr. Peters’ letters of the 7th
                    and 8th instants,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d979-f1"/> transmitting the reports of
                    the collector of customs at New York relative to the armament on the S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Giuseppe Verdi</hi> of the Transatlantica-Italiana Line,
                    and in reply to state that the Department is in receipt to-day of the formal
                    assurances of the Italian Ambassador that the guns on this vessel will be used
                    only for defensive purposes and will not be used to attacks submarine whilst
                    being warned. In these circumstances I have the honor to suggest that no
                    objection be raised to the clearance of the vessel on account of the armament
                    that she carries.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
